(8)
regulating the conduct of persons in respect of areas the control of which is considered necessary or expedient, and the
removal of persons from such areas;
(9)
requiring any person or class of persons to comply with any scheme of defence;
(10)
ensuring the safety of-----
(a)
ports, dockyards, lighthouses, light-ships and aerodromes;
(b)
railways, tramways, roads, bridges, canals and all other means of transport by land or water;
(c)
